.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The returned JSON string can be large if the session has many variables
or functions.
The \f[CR]\(dqvars\(dq\f[R] query in particular may return hundreds of
entries for a typical bash session that includes environment variables.
.IP \(bu 2
The JSON response is a single string, not a parsed data structure.
The caller must use a JSON parsing library (e.g., cJSON, jansson) to
extract individual entries.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]\(dqvars\(dq\f[R] query returns all variables including shell
built\-in variables (\f[CR]BASH_VERSION\f[R], \f[CR]RANDOM\f[R], etc.)
and environment variables.
There is no built\-in filtering mechanism; filter client\-side after
parsing.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]\(dqtraps\(dq\f[R] query only returns signals that have active
traps.
Signals at their default disposition are not listed.
.IP \(bu 2
For retrieving a single item by name, prefer the specific get functions
(\f[CR]bc_state_get_var\f[R], \f[CR]bc_state_get_func\f[R],
\f[CR]bc_state_get_alias\f[R]) which are more efficient than parsing the
full inspect output.
.IP \(bu 2
The returned string must be freed with \f[CR]bc_free()\f[R], not
standard \f[CR]free()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The function uses the v2 binary protocol internally.
The STATE channel request is a JSON object with
\f[CR]\(dqop\(dq: \(dqinspect\(dq\f[R] and \f[CR]\(dqquery\(dq\f[R]
fields.
.IP \(bu 2
A single \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R] must not be used concurrently from
multiple threads.
